    "## Assignment: Array Creation and Manipulation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "1. Create a NumPy array of shape (5, 5) filled with random integers between 1 and 20. Replace all the elements in the third column with 1.\n2. Create a NumPy array of shape (4, 4) with values from 1 to 16. Replace the diagonal elements with 0."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n\n# 1) (5,5) random ints 1-20; replace the third column (index 2) with 1\nnp.random.seed(101)\na = np.random.randint(1, 21, size=(5, 5))\nprint(\"Original 5x5 array (random 1-20):\"); print(a)\na[:, 2] = 1\nprint(\"After replacing 3rd column with 1:\"); print(a)\n\n# 2) (4,4) values 1-16; replace diagonal with 0\nnp.random.seed(102)\nb = np.arange(1, 17).reshape(4, 4)\nprint(\"Original 4x4 array:\"); print(b)\nnp.fill_diagonal(b, 0)\nprint(\"After replacing diagonal with 0:\"); print(b)\n"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
