    "## Assignment: Array Indexing and Slicing"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "1. Create a NumPy array of shape (6, 6) with values from 1 to 36. Extract the sub-array consisting of the 3rd to 5th rows and 2nd to 4th columns.\n2. Create a NumPy array of shape (5, 5) with random integers. Extract the elements on the border."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n\n# 1) (6,6) values 1..36; extract rows 3-5, cols 2-4 (0-based: 2:5, 1:4)\na = np.arange(1, 37).reshape(6, 6)\nsub = a[2:5, 1:4]\nprint(\"6x6 array:\"); print(a)\nprint(\"Sub-array (3rd-5th rows, 2nd-4th cols):\"); print(sub)\n\n# 2) (5,5) random; extract border elements (top row, left col, bottom row, right col)\nnp.random.seed(202)\nb = np.random.randint(1, 51, size=(5, 5))\nborder = np.concatenate([b[0], b[1:-1, 0], b[-1], b[1:-1, -1]])\nprint(\"5x5 random array:\"); print(b)\nprint(\"Border elements:\"); print(border)\n"
