    "## Assignment: Statistical Operations"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "1. Create a NumPy array of shape (5, 5) filled with random integers. Compute the mean, median, standard deviation, and variance of the array.\n2. Create a NumPy array of shape (3, 3) with values from 1 to 9. Normalize the array (i.e., scale the values to have a mean of 0 and a standard deviation of 1)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n\n# 1) (5,5) random; mean, median, std, variance\nnp.random.seed(404)\na = np.random.randint(1, 51, size=(5, 5))\nprint(\"5x5 array:\"); print(a)\nprint(\"Mean:\", a.mean())\nprint(\"Median:\", np.median(a))\nprint(\"Standard deviation:\", a.std())\nprint(\"Variance:\", a.var())\n\n# 2) (3,3) values 1..9; normalize to mean 0, std 1\nb = np.arange(1, 10).reshape(3, 3)\nb_norm = (b - b.mean()) / b.std()\nprint(\"Original 3x3:\"); print(b)\nprint(\"Normalized (mean 0, std 1):\"); print(np.round(b_norm, 3))\nprint(\"Normalized mean: %.6f | std: %.6f\" % (b_norm.mean(), b_norm.std()))\n"
   ],
